    "horizon_days": 7,
    "mechanism": "Large, unexpected volume spikes in thinly traded Indian stocks generate high price impact (high Amihud illiquidity). Market makers and algorithmic liquidity providers cannot instantly absorb the order flow due to inventory and risk limits, causing a temporary price overshoot that slowly reverts over a few days, yielding predictable excess returns.",
